The .py files in this directory are vendored verbatim from

    https://github.com/annasoligo/paper_gemma-needs-help  (evals/)

released under the MIT License by Anna Soligo, Vladimir Mikulik and William
Saunders, accompanying:

    Soligo, A., Mikulik, V. and Saunders, W. (2026). "Gemma Needs Help:
    Investigating and Mitigating Emotional Instability in LLMs."
    ICLR 2026 Workshop on From Human Cognition to AI Reasoning.
    arXiv:2603.10011

They are copied rather than paraphrased so our frustration numbers are
comparable to the paper's and to Conmy's, which uses the same protocol. Do not
edit them; if the protocol needs changing, change it in the caller
(scripts/rejection_rollout.py) and say so in the run's stats file.

The WildChat category described in the paper is not shipped upstream (it samples
allenai/WildChat-1M at eval time) and is therefore absent here too.
